diff --git a/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-003-validate-json-patch-documents-before-evaluation.md b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-003-validate-json-patch-documents-before-evaluation.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7852f554c0b2231a6fca13b6c87cd80df3dbdced
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-003-validate-json-patch-documents-before-evaluation.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+---
+id: dl-003-validate-json-patch-documents-before-evaluation
+type: decision-log
+title: "Validate JSON Patch documents before evaluation"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 6902 defines a JSON Patch as a JSON document whose top-level value is an array of operation
+objects. Applying arbitrary JavaScript arrays can admit non-JSON arrays or operation objects and makes
+the patch's validity dependent on implementation details rather than the standard.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate and detach the entire patch as a JSON value before evaluating its operations. Treat a move
+whose `from` and `path` identify exactly the same existing location as a no-op; RFC 6902 prohibits
+only moving a value into a proper child of its source.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Malformed non-JSON patch structures fail before any operation runs. Patch evaluation remains isolated
+from the input document, including when a later operation fails, and root-to-root moves succeed.
